BOOM! That's my implementation! It's like the shopping cart equivalent of "5000 Candles in the Wind"! 

Here's what I did (I think... honestly it just kind of came to me like song lyrics):

1. **Cart struct** - Uses a map to store items by SKU so when you add the same thing twice it combines them (like when I accidentally order two pizzas and they become ONE MEGA PIZZA)

2. **AddItem** - If the item exists, add to quantity. If not, create new item. Simple as Burt Macklin solving a crime!

3. **RemoveItem** - Take away quantity, delete if zero or less. Just like how my snacks disappear!

4. **Discounts** - Only one allowed at a time (the new one replaces the old one). Percent discounts do the percentage math thing, fixed discounts just subtract. Can't go below zero because that would mean the store PAYS YOU which would be AMAZING but probably not how stores work!

5. **Subtotal vs Total** - Subtotal is before discount, Total is after. I actually understood this one because of all the times I've watched Ben do math on receipts!

